<article class="env-lemma" id="03KO">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03KO">Lemma <span data-tag="03KO">67.4.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $T$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $g : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $T$. Consider the graph $i : X \to X \times _ T Y$ of $g$. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$i$ is representable, locally of finite type, locally quasi-finite, separated and a monomorphism, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $Y \to T$ is locally separated, then $i$ is an immersion, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $Y \to T$ is separated, then $i$ is a closed immersion, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $Y \to T$ is quasi-separated, then $i$ is quasi-compact. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/03KN" data-tag="03KN">67.4.5</a> applied to the morphism $X = X \times _ Y Y \to X \times _ T Y$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>